  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN237.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉkaṇ vēṟupaṭṭa talaimakaḷait tōḻi vaṟpuṟuttiyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">How the confidante consoled HER who had undergone changes during the separation from HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN237.1">
        <l>puṉkāṟ pātiri mariniṟat tiraḷvī</l>
        <l>nuṇkoṭi yatiraloṭu nuṇaṅkaṟal varippa</l>
        <l>varaveyiṟ ṟaṉṉa varumpumutir kuraviṉ</l>
        <l>ṟēṉimir naṟuñciṉait teṉṟal pōḻak</l>
        <l>kuyilkural kaṟṟa vēṉilun tuyi<supplied>ṟu</supplied>ṟan</l>
        <l>tiṉṉā kaḻiyuṅ kaṅku leṉṟuniṉ</l>
        <l>ṉaṉmā mēṉi yaṇinalam pulampa</l>
        <l>viṉaita lāṉṟici ṉāyiḻai<anchor n="1"/> kaṉaiteṟaṟ</l>
        <l>cēr<supplied>tī</supplied> yaṇaṅkiya ceḻuniṇak koḻuṅkuṟai</l>
        <l>meṉṟiṉaip puṉka mutirtta maṇṭaiyō</l>
        <l>ṭiruṅkati ra<supplied>la</supplied>maruṅ kaḻaṉik karumpiṉ</l>
        <l>viḷaikaḻai piḻinta vantīñ cēṟṟoṭu</l>
        <l>pālpey cenneṟ pācavaṟ pakukkum</l>
        <l>puṉalporu putavi ṉuṟantaiyeytiṉum</l>
        <l>viṉaiporu ḷākat taviralar kaṭaici<supplied>va</supplied>n</l>
        <l>taiya vamartta vuṇkaṇiṉ</l>
        <l>vaiyēr vāleyiṟ ṟūṟiya nīrē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">While the round blossoms with fading colour of the low-stemmed trumpet-flower tree</l>
        <l corresp="2">together with the wild jasmine in fine creepers line the fine black sand,</l>
        <l corresp="4">while the south wind crosses the honey[-bee]-humming fragrant branches</l>
        <l corresp="3">of the bottle-flower tree on which buds mature that are like snake’s teeth,</l>
        <l corresp="5">even in summer when the koel practices [its] tune, abandoning sleep,</l>
        <l corresp="6">saying “the night will pass in an unpleasant way,”</l>
        <l corresp="7">while the adorning beauty of your good dark body is lonely,</l>
        <l corresp="8a-c">stop being desperate, [you with] choice jewels.</l>
        <l corresp="14">Even if he were to attain Uṟantai against whose gate the flood dashes,</l>
        <l>where, along with bowls in which fat pieces [of meat] with ample fat</l>
        <l corresp="8d-10">fried in fire with intense heat are strewn on boiled grains of soft millet,</l>
        <l corresp="13">they distribute fresh rice from red paddy on which milk is poured</l>
        <l corresp="12">with pretty sweet pulp that is pressed from the ripe shafts</l>
        <l corresp="11">of sugarcane from [near] the paddy fields where large ears are quivering,</l>
        <l corresp="15a-c">he will not be detained since his task is wealth,</l>
        <l corresp="17">– [on account of] the water that oozes from [between] your sharp fine white teeth,</l>
        <l corresp="15d-16">[you with] kajal eyes that are wonderfully at strife , [their] rims reddened.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

